    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay but it feels like most of that \"empirical evidence\" just comes from studies that are already predisposed to favor DEI. a lot of people are pretty much saying that the whole thing is just a way to avoid lawsuits or look good in PR rather than actually helping the company grow. do you think there's a legitimate case to be made that companies would actually be more efficient if they just focused on meritocracy without these extra programs?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
